{
 "id": "remote_operate",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "area": "retina",
 "description": "PERFORM THE ACTION ON THE CROSS (block 230000): exhaust the ACTION space on the reached object and DISCOVER the actuating action. Extends the 226/228 exhaustion principle from the OBJECT space to the ACTION space: at the reached object, try EVERY available action ON it \u2014 the movement actions AND the interact/use action (210 op_use) \u2014 because 'tried everything' is not complete until it has tried ACTING on the thing, not just moving into it. ro_try_action (policy exhaust_actions) picks the min-ordinal untried GameAction (exactly one per pass) and issues it; ro_try_movement (policy movement_only, the CONTROL) tries only movements; ro_discover_operate mints Operates{action,object,effect} from an ActionOutcome that OBSERVED a remote change \u2014 the actuating action DISCOVERED from the observed outcome, never hardcoded. Composes with 229 UNCHANGED: the Observation the adapter writes when the actuating action fires is consumed by rcg_ground -> causes(object,effect). Domain-agnostic (no cross/rotation/action-id constant; the id + effect carried from the OBSERVED outcome). Guarded on game.operate_on==1 (default-OFF, byte-identical) + game.op_policy. Integer-native; no Rust; reuses 210 operate + 228 reach + 229 ground + 220 nav.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "remote_operate",
  "description": "'Tried everything' includes ACTING ON the thing, not just moving into it. At the reached object the agent exhausts the ACTION space \u2014 every available action, the interact/use action too \u2014 and DISCOVERS which one actuates it by OBSERVING which produces a remote change. The actuator is discovered from observation, never hardcoded; the elicited change is what 229 grounds. Every decision is a rule; the adapter only issues the chosen action and perceives the result."
 },
